# steps/merge-callable-r48.md S1: a held callable -- add5, a root own holding makeAdder's merged node -- called from a
# method, as a value and on the right of && (a guarded call), through the same l2_mad_call helper the root's walk
# calls.  Before S1 the method's call left the translator without a word (exit 3, "a refusal said nothing").  6 and
# 6: entry 7.
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: n + x
    return: addN
add5: makeAdder 5
fn: go () int
    int: a (add5: 1)
    int: ok 0
    if: a = 6 && (add5: 1) = 6
        ok: 7
    return: ok
int: r 0
r: go()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
